write a python script to compile a .c or .cpp file
example usage:
python mkc.py file.c
python mkc.py file.cpp
if input is .c file, script should run
clang <fname> -o <fname without extension(which is .c)>
via subprocess
if input is .cpp file, script should run
clang++ <fname> -o <fname without extension(which is .cpp)>
via subprocess
if compile successful, run (strip <output>)
input=sys.argv[1]
